  "text": "Here is the polite way to schedule global remote calls without burning out your staff. Always expecting offshore team members to adapt to headquarters hours creates resentment and silent quitting. Unequal scheduling culture forces remote employees to attend late night calls while headquarters operates in comfort. Set up an automated rotation policy in Google Calendar that alternates meeting host timezones every month. This builds genuine team equity across continents.",
